{"headword":"גִּלְעָד","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.pr.loc.</strong> of mountain-range or hill-country, land & city, E. of Jordan <strong>(</strong>cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">جَلْعَدٌ</span> <em>durus, fortis</em> Frey, so Thes; Hi<sup>Gesch. Isr. 26</sup> comp. same √ used of <em>camel</em> (<span dir=\"rtl\">جَلْعَادٌ</span> <em>camelus robustus ac firmus</em>, cf. Hom<sup>NS 144</sup>), whence <em>camel hump</em>, orig. name of mt<strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 37:25\" href=\"/Genesis.37.25\">Gn 37:25</a> + 79 times (mostly as <strong>n.pr.m.</strong> and in combin. with other <strong>n.pr.loc.</strong> cf. infr.); <span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:21\" href=\"/Genesis.31.21\">Gn 31:21</a> + 50 times (so usually as name of mt. and land); <span dir=\"rtl\">גִּלְעָ֫דָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:39\" href=\"/Numbers.32.39\">Nu 32:39</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:21\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.21\">1 Ch 27:21</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הִגְּלְעָ֫דָה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.6\">2 S 24:6</a>;—<em>Gilead</em>, used of territory between the Arnon and the Jabboḳ, mod. <em>Belḳa;</em> also of that between the Jabboḳ and the Jarmuk, mod. <em>Jebel Ajlûn;</em> also of the entire E.-Jordan land occupied by Israel, including both the parts just named (cf. Di <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:54\" href=\"/Genesis.31.54\">Gn 31:54</a> Stu <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:4\" href=\"/Judges.10.4\">Ju 10:4</a>; Bd<sup>Pal. 178</sup>; also L. Oliphant<sup>Land of Gilead, 1880</sup>);—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"territory S. of Jabboḳ,"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:29\" href=\"/Numbers.32.29\">Nu 32:29</a> (P), <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ ג׳</span> v<a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:1\" href=\"/Numbers.32.1\">1</a> (JE), both connected with Reuben and Gad; so <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲצִי הַר הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:12\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.12\">Dt 3:12</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ ג׳</span> also <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 5:9\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.5.9\">1 Ch 5:9</a> (of Reuben); <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:19\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.19\">1 K 4:19</a> (of Sihon and Og); cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ גַּד וְג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 13:7\" href=\"/I_Samuel.13.7\">1 S 13:7</a>; further,"}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> alone, <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:17\" href=\"/Judges.10.17\">Ju 10:17</a> (or possibly here name of city?), <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:29\" href=\"/Judges.11.29\">11:29</a> (prob.); also <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 5:10\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.5.10\">1 Ch 5:10</a> (of Reuben) v <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 5:16\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.5.16\">16</a> (of Gad); cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲצִי הַגּ׳ וְעַד יַבֹּק</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 12:2\" href=\"/Joshua.12.2\">Jos 12:2</a> (of Sihon), so v <a data-ref=\"Joshua 12:5\" href=\"/Joshua.12.5\">5</a> (both D);"}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"similarly <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span> alone (without art.) in poet. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 60:9\" href=\"/Psalms.60.9\">ψ 60:9</a> (‖ Manasseh) = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 108:9\" href=\"/Psalms.108.9\">108:9</a>; but also in prose in phrases <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂרֵי ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:18\" href=\"/Judges.10.18\">Ju 10:18</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ישְׁבֵי ג׳</span> v <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:18\" href=\"/Judges.10.18\">18</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:8\" href=\"/Judges.11.8\">11:8</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">זִקְנֵי ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:5\" href=\"/Judges.11.5\">Ju 11:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:7\" href=\"/Judges.11.7\">7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:8\" href=\"/Judges.11.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:9\" href=\"/Judges.11.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:10\" href=\"/Judges.11.10\">10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:11\" href=\"/Judges.11.11\">11</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַנְשֵׁי ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:4\" href=\"/Judges.12.4\">Ju 12:4</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:5\" href=\"/Judges.12.5\">5</a>; cf. also"}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">עָרֵי הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:26\" href=\"/Numbers.32.26\">Nu 32:26</a> (JE; of Reuben and Gad); so of Jephthah’s burial-place <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:7\" href=\"/Judges.12.7\">Ju 12:7</a>; even <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּל־עָרֵי הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:25\" href=\"/Joshua.13.25\">Jos 13:25</a> (P; of Gad); besides these, of particular cities, especially <span dir=\"rtl\">רָאמֹת בַּגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:43\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.43\">Dt 4:43</a> (of Gad); cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">רָאמוֹת בַּגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 20:8\" href=\"/Joshua.20.8\">Jos 20:8</a> (P), <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 6:65\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.6.65\">1 Ch 6:65</a> (of Gad), and <span dir=\"rtl\">רָמֹת בַּגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:38\" href=\"/Joshua.21.38\">Jos 21:38</a> (P); usually <span dir=\"rtl\">רָמֹת ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:13\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.13\">1 K 4:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:3\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.3\">22:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:4\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:6\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.6\">6</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:12\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:15\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.15\">15</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.29\">29</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:2\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.2\">2 Ch 18:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:3\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.3\">3</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:11\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:14\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.14\">14</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:19\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:28\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.28\">28</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 8:28\" href=\"/II_Kings.8.28\">2 K 8:28</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:1\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.1\">9:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:4\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:14\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.14\">14</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 22:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.22.5\">2 Ch 22:5</a>; also <span dir=\"rtl\">מִצְפֵּה ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:29\" href=\"/Judges.11.29\">Ju 11:29</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; further <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעְזֵיר ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 26:31\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.26.31\">1 Ch 26:31</a>."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Northern Gilead,"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 17:5\" href=\"/Joshua.17.5\">Jos 17:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 17:6\" href=\"/Joshua.17.6\">6</a> (JE; of Manasseh) cf. <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:4\" href=\"/Judges.10.4\">Ju 10:4</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:22\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.22\">1 Ch 2:22</a> (both of Jair); <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:21\" href=\"/Genesis.31.21\">Gn 31:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:23\" href=\"/Genesis.31.23\">23</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:25\" href=\"/Genesis.31.25\">25</a> (E); prob. also <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר ג׳</span> (no art.) <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.1\">Ct 4:1</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:5\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.5\">6:5</a> infr.)."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> alone <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:40\" href=\"/Numbers.32.40\">Nu 32:40</a> (JE; of Machir) <a data-ref=\"Joshua 17:1\" href=\"/Joshua.17.1\">Jos 17:1</a> (JE; <em>id.</em>) cf. <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:11\" href=\"/Joshua.13.11\">13:11</a> (D) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:36\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.36\">Dt 2:36</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:13\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.13\">1 K 4:13</a> (of Jair); <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.15\">Dt 3:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:16\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.16\">16</a> (boundary of Reuben and Gad); prob. also <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:5\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.5\">Ct 6:5</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.1\">4:1</a> supr.); cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יֶתֶר הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.13\">Dt 3:13</a>; & <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲצִי הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:31\" href=\"/Joshua.13.31\">Jos 13:31</a> (P; of Machir); <span dir=\"rtl\">הַגִּלְעָ֫דָה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.6\">2 S 24:6</a> (prob.); cf. also"}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span> (no art.) prob. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 8:22\" href=\"/Jeremiah.8.22\">Je 8:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 46:11\" href=\"/Jeremiah.46.11\">46:11</a> (in both ref. to <span dir=\"rtl\">צֳרִי</span> <em>balm</em>, prob. from the wooded Northern Gilead); similarly <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 22:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.22.6\">22:6</a>; and <span dir=\"rtl\">גִּלְעָ֫דָה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:21\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.21\">1 Ch 27:21</a>, also <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:39\" href=\"/Numbers.32.39\">Nu 32:39</a> (JE; of Machir)."}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"in combination <span dir=\"rtl\">יָבֵשׁ ג׳</span> (city) <a data-ref=\"Judges 21:8\" href=\"/Judges.21.8\">Ju 21:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 21:9\" href=\"/Judges.21.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 21:10\" href=\"/Judges.21.10\">10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 21:12\" href=\"/Judges.21.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 21:14\" href=\"/Judges.21.14\">14</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 11:1\" href=\"/I_Samuel.11.1\">1 S 11:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 11:9\" href=\"/I_Samuel.11.9\">9</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יָבֵשׁ</span> alone) <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 31:11\" href=\"/I_Samuel.31.11\">31:11</a> (‖ <em>id.</em>) = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 10:11\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.10.11\">1 Ch 10:11</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:4\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.4\">2 S 2:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.5\">5</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 21:12\" href=\"/II_Samuel.21.12\">21:12</a>; perhaps also <span dir=\"rtl\">(מִ)תִּשְׁבֵּה ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 17:1\" href=\"/I_Kings.17.1\">1 K 17:1</a> (emend., after 𝔊, Ew Th al. see VB);—cf. further sub <strong>6</strong>. <strong>n.pr.m.</strong> infr.—<a data-ref=\"Judges 7:3\" href=\"/Judges.7.3\">Ju 7:3</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וְיִצְפֹּר מֵהַר הַגּ׳</span> <em>and let him depart from Mt. Gilead</em>, appar. belongs here, but <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵהַר הַגִּלְבֹּעַ</span> is read by Cler Hi Gr Ke Be; against this cf. Stu Bu<sup>RS 112</sup>."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"more generally, of all Gilead,"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 22:9\" href=\"/Joshua.22.9\">Jos 22:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 22:13\" href=\"/Joshua.22.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 22:15\" href=\"/Joshua.22.15\">15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 22:32\" href=\"/Joshua.22.32\">32</a> (P; of Reuben, Gad and Manasseh; opp. land of Canaan); cf. <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:26\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.26\">2 S 17:26</a>; so <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּל־אֶרֶץ הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 10:33\" href=\"/II_Kings.10.33\">2 K 10:33</a>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ ג׳</span> (no art.) <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 10:10\" href=\"/Zechariah.10.10\">Zc 10:10</a>; cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר אֶפְרַיִם וְג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:19\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.19\">Je 50:19</a> (‖ Carmel and Bashan); <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span> alone, also <a data-ref=\"Genesis 37:25\" href=\"/Genesis.37.25\">Gn 37:25</a>; likewise <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:14\" href=\"/Micah.7.14\">Mi 7:14</a> (‖ Carmel & Bashan, reference to fertility)."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> alone, of Isr. territ. in gen. E. of Jordan, <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:8\" href=\"/Judges.10.8\">Ju 10:8</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:9\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.9\">2 S 2:9</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 10:33\" href=\"/II_Kings.10.33\">2 K 10:33</a> (of Reuben, Gad and Manasseh); <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּל־הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.10\">Dt 3:10</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶת־כָּל־הָאָרֶץ אֶת־הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 34:1\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.34.1\">Dt 34:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> also in general sense <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 47:18\" href=\"/Ezekiel.47.18\">Ez 47:18</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 15:29\" href=\"/II_Kings.15.29\">2 K 15:29</a>(?) <a data-ref=\"Obadiah 1:19\" href=\"/Obadiah.1.19\">Ob 19</a>."}],"num":"c."}],"num":"3."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span>, name of a city <a data-ref=\"Hosea 6:8\" href=\"/Hosea.6.8\">Ho 6:8</a> (& <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:17\" href=\"/Judges.10.17\">Ju 10:17</a>? cf. <strong>1 a.</strong> supr.);—on the ruined cities <em>Jilʿâd, Jilʿaud</em> on the <em>Jebel Jilʿâd</em>, N. of Es-Salṭ, and S. of Jabboḳ v. Di <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:54\" href=\"/Genesis.31.54\">Gn 31:54</a> & reff."}],"num":"4."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">אֶרֶץ הַגּ׳</span> of Israelites living E. of Jordan (as a whole) <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:1\" href=\"/Judges.20.1\">Ju 20:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> of people of Gilead <a data-ref=\"Amos 1:3\" href=\"/Amos.1.3\">Am 1:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Amos 1:13\" href=\"/Amos.1.13\">13</a>; so <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:17\" href=\"/Judges.5.17\">Ju 5:17</a> (= <span dir=\"rtl\">גַּד</span>), <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:4\" href=\"/Judges.12.4\">12:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:5\" href=\"/Judges.12.5\">5</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אַנְשֵׁי ג׳</span> v <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:4\" href=\"/Judges.12.4\">4</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:5\" href=\"/Judges.12.5\">5</a>) <a data-ref=\"Hosea 12:12\" href=\"/Hosea.12.12\">Ho 12:12</a>. Cf. also <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, גִּלְעָדִי\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_גִּלְעָדִי\">גִּלְעָדִי</a> infr."}],"num":"5."},{"senses":[{"definition":"treated as <strong>n.pr.m. </strong>"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳</span>, son of Machir & grandson of Manasseh <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:29\" href=\"/Numbers.26.29\">Nu 26:29</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:30\" href=\"/Numbers.26.30\">30</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 27:1\" href=\"/Numbers.27.1\">27:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 36:1\" href=\"/Numbers.36.1\">36:1</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 17:3\" href=\"/Joshua.17.3\">Jos 17:3</a> (all P) <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:21\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.21\">1 Ch 2:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:23\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 7:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.7.14\">7:14</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 7:17\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.7.17\">17</a>; once <span dir=\"rtl\">הַגּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 17:1\" href=\"/Joshua.17.1\">Jos 17:1</a> (JE) cf. Di;—ref. in all these to Northern Gilead."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"father of Jephthah <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:1\" href=\"/Judges.11.1\">Ju 11:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:2\" href=\"/Judges.11.2\">2</a>;—ref. to Gad (cf. supr. especially sub <strong>5</strong>)."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 5:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.5.14\">1 Ch 5:14</a> (a Gadite)."}],"num":"c."}],"num":"6."}]},"rid":"BDB01853","strong_numbers":["1568"],"next_hw":"גִּלְעָדִי","prev_hw":"גַּלְעֵד²","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["1680"],"TWOT":["356"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":t